<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<worksheet xml:id="mth108-distributing-combining">
<title>Distributing and Combining</title>
<objectives>
<ul>
<li>I can use the distributive property, including with negative numbers and a negative sign in front of parentheses, and then combine like terms to simplify an expression.</li>
</ul>
</objectives>

<introduction>
<p><em>Simplify each expression below. Review the example provided before each section. Show your steps in the blank space provided.</em></p>
</introduction>

<page>
<example xml:id="dc-example-distributing">
<title>Distributing a Value</title>
<p>When a number is directly outside parentheses, we multiply it by <em>every</em> term inside. Pay special attention to negative signs!</p>
<p><em>Positive:</em><md>4(3x - 2) \quad \longrightarrow \quad 4(3x) - 4(2) \quad \longrightarrow \quad 12x - 8</md></p>
<p><em>Negative:</em><md>-5(2x - 3) \quad \longrightarrow \quad -5(2x) - (-5)(3) \quad \longrightarrow \quad -10x + 15</md></p>
</example>

<exercise xml:id="dc-distribute-positive" workspace="1.5in">
<title>Problem 1</title>
<statement>
<p>Distribute to simplify the expression.<md>6(2x - 5)</md></p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>Multiply both <m>2x</m> and <m>-5</m> by <m>6</m>:<md>6(2x) - 6(5) = 12x - 30</md></p>
</answer>
</exercise>

<exercise xml:id="dc-distribute-negative" workspace="1.75in">
<title>Problem 2</title>
<statement>
<p>Distribute the negative value to simplify.<md>-3(4 - 5x)</md></p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>Multiply both <m>4</m> and <m>-5x</m> by <m>-3</m>:<md>-3(4) - (-3)(5x) = -12 + 15x</md></p>
<p>This can also be written as <m>15x - 12</m>.</p>
</answer>
</exercise>

<example xml:id="dc-example-invisible-one">
<title>The Invisible <m>-1</m></title>
<p>If there is only a negative sign in front of the parentheses, treat it as distributing a <m>-1</m>. This flips the sign of everything inside.<md>-(x - 7) \quad \longrightarrow \quad -1(x - 7) \quad \longrightarrow \quad -x + 7</md></p>
</example>

<exercise xml:id="dc-negative-sign-1" workspace="1.5in">
<title>Problem 3</title>
<statement>
<p>Simplify by distributing the negative sign.<md>-(3x + 8)</md></p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>Treat the negative sign as <m>-1</m>:<md>-1(3x + 8) = -3x - 8</md></p>
</answer>
</exercise>

<exercise xml:id="dc-negative-sign-2" workspace="1.5in">
<title>Problem 4</title>
<statement>
<p>Simplify by distributing the negative sign.<md>-(-x - 4)</md></p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>Treat the negative sign as <m>-1</m>. Both terms inside are negative, so both become positive:<md>-1(-x - 4) = x + 4</md></p>
</answer>
</exercise>
</page>

<page>
<example xml:id="dc-example-together">
<title>Putting It Together</title>
<p>A helpful strategy is to distribute first, then combine your like terms (group your <m>x</m>'s together, and your regular numbers together).</p>
<p>Distribute the <m>-2</m>:<md>10x - 2(x + 4) + 5 \quad \longrightarrow \quad 10x - 2x - 8 + 5</md></p>
<p>Combine like terms:<md>10x - 2x - 8 + 5 \quad \longrightarrow \quad 8x - 3</md></p>
</example>

<exercise xml:id="dc-combine-1" workspace="2in">
<title>Problem 5</title>
<statement>
<p>Simplify the expression using any method you like. Show your work.<md>12x - 3(4 - 2x) + 9</md></p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>Distribute the <m>-3</m>:<md>12x - 12 + 6x + 9</md></p>
<p>Group the like terms together:<md>12x + 6x - 12 + 9</md></p>
<p>Combine the like terms:<md>18x - 3</md></p>
</answer>
</exercise>

<exercise xml:id="dc-combine-2" workspace="2in">
<title>Problem 6</title>
<statement>
<p>Simplify the expression. Watch out for the negative sign!<md>7 + 4x - (x - 2)</md></p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>Distribute the negative sign to both terms inside the parentheses:<md>7 + 4x - x + 2</md></p>
<p>Group the like terms together:<md>4x - x + 7 + 2</md></p>
<p>Combine the like terms:<md>3x + 9</md></p>
<p>Be careful with the last term. Subtracting <m>-2</m> is the same as adding <m>2</m>.</p>
</answer>
</exercise>

<example xml:id="dc-example-variable-types">
<title>Keeping Variable Types Separate</title>
<p>Terms with <m>x^2</m> are completely different from terms with <m>x</m>. You cannot combine them together.<md>3x^2 + 5x - 2x^2 - x \quad \longrightarrow \quad (3x^2 - 2x^2) + (5x - 1x) \quad \longrightarrow \quad x^2 + 4x</md></p>
</example>

<exercise xml:id="dc-combine-3" workspace="2.5in">
<title>Problem 7</title>
<statement>
<p>Simplify the following expression. Group your <m>x^2</m> terms, your <m>x</m> terms, and your constant numbers.<md>5x^2 + 2x - 7 + 3(x^2 - 4x + 2)</md></p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>Distribute the <m>3</m>:<md>5x^2 + 2x - 7 + 3x^2 - 12x + 6</md></p>
<p>Group the like terms together:<md>5x^2 + 3x^2 + 2x - 12x - 7 + 6</md></p>
<p>Combine the like terms:<md>8x^2 - 10x - 1</md></p>
</answer>
</exercise>
</page>

</worksheet>
